 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
6	Subsequent to the quarter ended 30 June 2026,  all outstanding Compulsorily Convertible Debentures amounting to Rs. 1,500 Millions issued by our Company to HDFC Capital Affordable Real Estate Fund – 3, together with accrued interest thereon amounting to Rs. 671.87 Millions, were converted into equity shares at a conversion price of Rs. 342.49, resulting in the issuance of 6,341,436 equity shares.  &lt;br /&gt; 
 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
7	Subsequent to the quarter ended 30 June 2026, the NCLT approved the Scheme of Demerger between Evie Real Estate Private Limited and Evie Developers Private Limited (subsidiaries of the Company)  via its order dated 28 July 2026. The Scheme has an appointed date of 1 April 2026, and requires accounting under the pooling of interests method in accordance with Appendix C to Ind AS 103. The financial impact of the Scheme is recognised effective from the appointed date 1 April 2026, in accordance with the approved Scheme and applicable accounting standards. &lt;br /&gt; 
 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
8	During the period, two subsidiaries of the Company, received compensation aggregating to Rs. 1,852.56 Millions, comprising principal compensation and interest thereon, in respect of land acquired at Usarghar, Kalyan, District Thane, Maharashtra, for the Virar–Alibaug Multimodal Corridor project. The compensation has been accounted for in the books of subsidiaries in accordance with the applicable accounting principles and based on the relevant supporting documentation. &lt;br /&gt; 
 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
9	The Group is primarily engaged in the business of real estate development, which is considered as the only reportable business segment. Further, the Group's revenue is derived primarily from sale of residential and commerical units. Also, the Group operates within India and does not have operations in economic environments with different risks and returns. Hence, it is considered operating in a single geographical segment. Accordingly, there are no other separate reportable segments in terms of Ind AS 108 on "Operating Segment". &lt;br /&gt; 
 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
10	 The figures for the year ended 31 March 2026 have been extracted from the general purpose Consolidated Financial Statement which were audited by the Statutory Auditors of the Company. The figures for the quarter ended March 2026 are the balancing figures between the audited figures in respect of the full financial year ended 31 March 2026 and the unaudited year to date figures upto period ended 31 December 2025, which were neither subject to Limited Review nor Audit. However, the management has exercised necessary care and due diligence to ensure that the consolidated financial results for that period are fairly stated.  &lt;br /&gt; 
 	 					  &lt;br /&gt; 
11	The figures for the corresponding previous periods have been regrouped and reclassified wherever necessary, to make them comparable.  &lt;br /&gt; 
